.TH SYS_PROC_CWD 2 "2026-03-05" "Substrate" "System Calls Manual"
.SH NAME
sys_proc_cwd \- query process current working directory
.SH LIBRARY
System library (libsys, \-lsys)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <sys/sysinfo.h>
.PP
.BI "int sys_proc_cwd(pid_t " pid ", char *" buf ", size_t " len ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR sys_proc_cwd ()
attempts to copy the current working directory path of process
.IR pid 
into
.IR buf .
At most
.I len
bytes are written including the terminating NUL.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, 0 is returned.
On error, a negated errno is returned.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EFAULT
.I buf
is NULL or points outside the caller's address space, or
.I len
is zero.
.TP
.B EPERM
The caller is not root, and the process is not its own: its real or
effective user id differs from the caller's effective one, or it has
changed credentials (set-id exec).
.TP
.B ERANGE
.I len
is too small for the path and its NUL.
.TP
.B ESRCH
.I pid
does not refer to an existing process.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR getcwd (2),
.BR sys_proc_exe (2),
.BR sys_proc_info (2)
